WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:03.300
What do you think about Sabo and what has
happened to him?

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:09.320
What if I told you that he is bringing Vivi
and the Revolutionaries to Luffy right this

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:10.320
moment?

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.089
That he will be more important to the story
than Ace.

00:00:13.089 --> 00:00:16.859
And that I've actually shed a tear while writing
this script?

00:00:16.859 --> 00:00:22.220
Actually on second thought, don't answer that.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:27.560
Okay, real talk for a second.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.960
As you know, the reason I love One Piece so
much is not because of the fights or the powers

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.930
or even the world building.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:37.730
All of these are absolutely fantastic, no
question about it.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:45.430
But to me, what puts One Piece above other
great works of fiction is its out-of-this-world

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:46.430
character writing.

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:51.160
Not only does the story have one of the biggest
cast of characters ever, but pretty much every

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:56.690
single one of them has their own personality,
development and purpose in the story.

00:00:56.690 --> 00:01:01.530
Everyone feels like they belong into this
world and each and every one of them does

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:06.000
their part to make One Piece the epic adventure
it is.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.640
Which brings me back to Sabo.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:12.920
I have wanted to talk about Sabo for a while
now, because in a weird way he seems to be

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:17.440
the odd one out here, not just for me, but
for many others as well.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:22.620
The amnesia plot-line was not very well received,
I mean you can't tell me Sabo never saw an

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:27.140
image of Ace in the newspaper before, and
in many ways, Sabo's only role can easily

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:37.270
be mistaken as a replacement for Ace.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:42.020
And objectively speaking, at this point in
the story, if nothing else happened with him,

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:47.590
I would go so far as to call him the only
bad character in the story, because he doesn't

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:50.130
really contribute to Luffy's story.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:55.840
However, and this is where this video turns
positive, I finally realised that by thinking

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:01.980
this way I might not only have judged Sabo's
role in the story extremely prematurely, but

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:07.920
even worse, I probably have actually drastically
underestimated the potential Sabo has for

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.720
Luffy and the endgame of the story.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:16.060
Hi, my name is Manu and as an older brother
myself, I think I have finally figured out

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:21.700
what Sabo's character is all about, what has
happened to him during the Reverie and what

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:24.480
role he has to play at the end of the story.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:29.489
Despite being one of the most influential
people in Luffy's life, I was surprised how

00:02:29.489 --> 00:02:32.909
late in the story Sabo was introduced.

00:02:32.909 --> 00:02:37.870
The first time we learn about his existence
is during Luffy's flashback after the end

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:40.209
of Marineford.

00:02:40.209 --> 00:02:49.519
I 
have seen a lot of people speculate that Oda

00:02:49.519 --> 00:02:54.749
just wrote Sabo into the story at that point
on a whim, but I'm convinced that Sabo was

00:02:54.749 --> 00:03:00.569
part of Oda's plans right from the start,
which is also why I'm not worried about him

00:03:00.569 --> 00:03:02.680
being a character without purpose.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:05.739
Here is some of the early foreshadowing by
Oda.

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:10.799
His first possible appearance might have been
in chapter 99, where we see someone looking

00:03:10.799 --> 00:03:15.910
suspicipously like sabo in the crowd as Buggy
plans to execute Luffy.

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:21.439
This would make further sense, because it
is also Dragon's first appearance in the story.

00:03:21.439 --> 00:03:26.109
Next we have the flashback of Luffy and Ace
sharing Sake to become brothers, and as you

00:03:26.109 --> 00:03:31.859
can see in the top left corner, there is a
third cup, just barely visible.

00:03:31.859 --> 00:03:36.389
Another hint, that hit me really hard when
I realised what it meant, was Ace's Tatoo,

00:03:36.389 --> 00:03:39.200
that we first get to see in Alabasta.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:43.889
At first glance it looks like he found himself
the worlds worst tattoo artist, that managed

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:46.099
to misspell ace with an s.

00:03:46.099 --> 00:03:55.799
But then, we saw Sabo set out to sea [sabo
and his Jolly Roger leaving goa].

00:03:55.799 --> 00:04:02.779
It's not a strike through S, ace has literally
tattooed Sabo's Jolly Roger on his arm as

00:04:02.779 --> 00:04:08.689
a tribute, from the last time he saw his brother,
before seeing him die at the hands of the

00:04:08.689 --> 00:04:10.540
celestial dragons.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:13.529
Gotta be real, I teared up there a little
when I learned that.

00:04:13.529 --> 00:04:19.019
So, I hope you agree that most likely Sabo
was always part of Oda's plan.

00:04:19.019 --> 00:04:21.970
What then is his purpose in the story?

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:24.300
Is merely being a replacement for Ace?

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:30.960
And the answer to that is nyaaaa-kind of but
not really, but definitely in a good way.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:35.020
Okay so: Sabo actually has three important
roles in the story.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:42.270
For the first of these we have to go back
all the way to Luffy's childhood.

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:51.479
Sabo shaped both Luffy and Ace into the great
pirates that they later would become.

00:04:51.479 --> 00:04:56.490
Ace, suffering under his heritage, was always
in a very dark place.

00:04:56.490 --> 00:05:02.720
It was only thanks to sabo, that he was able
to find someone he could truly trust and forget

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.319
his worries with.

00:05:04.319 --> 00:05:10.169
On top of this, Sabo served as the relaxed
and positive moderator between him and Luffy,

00:05:10.169 --> 00:05:13.389
as both were very head-strong and impulsive.

00:05:13.389 --> 00:05:18.800
In my opinion, Sabo might well be part of
the reason Luffy is so incredibly tolerant

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:20.349
toward everyone.

00:05:20.349 --> 00:05:25.110
Even though they were living in poverty in
the shadow of the nobles, Sabo, who was a

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:29.370
noble himself, was just a friend and brother
to Luffy.

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:34.920
It taught him that a person is made by their
actions and not their heritage.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:40.090
Even better, since Sabo was well-educated,
he most likely contributed most of the knowledge

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:42.590
that Luffy and Ace got as children.

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:50.139
But most importantly, Sabo was one of the
key factors, that inspired both Ace and Luffy

00:05:50.139 --> 00:05:52.699
to become great pirates.

00:05:52.699 --> 00:05:55.909
Shanks was definitely a major driver for luffy
as well.

00:05:55.909 --> 00:06:01.490
However I feel like it is this scene here,
when Luffy learns about Sabo's death for the

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:08.080
first time, where a lot of Luffy's ideals
and even his dream can be traced back to.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:19.610
[do you think sabo was happy / luffy saying
: he really wasn't happy]

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:25.219
Luffy realising that sabo tried to become
a pirate in order to find happiness is basically

00:06:25.219 --> 00:06:28.979
the premise for each and every one of his
crew mates.

00:06:28.979 --> 00:06:34.060
He finds great people that just like Sabo
have been in an incredibly dark spot their

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:40.419
entire life, and gives them true freedom and
happiness by making them pirates of his crew.

00:06:40.419 --> 00:06:46.110
Luffy goes out of his way to pull people out
of their darkness, because of Sabo's death

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:52.610
and how he and Ace did not realize it, did
not try to help him escape his terrible family.

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:57.999
This of course is also connected to Ace's
death, where Luffy now feels like he had failed

00:06:57.999 --> 00:07:01.819
to save not only one, but two brothers.

00:07:01.819 --> 00:07:12.370
And it's exactly that subtext, that makes
Luffy's reunion with Sabo so special.

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:19.599
Now the only arc, where Sabo had a chance
to showcase his current personality so far,

00:07:19.599 --> 00:07:20.599
is Dressrosa.

00:07:20.599 --> 00:07:24.470
A big criticism I often hear is that Sabo
is basically just ace 2.0.

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:28.360
And in a way, these people have a point.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:33.509
Both of them have similar 'cool older brother
vibes', both are powerful members of two of

00:07:33.509 --> 00:07:39.550
the most influentail groups in the story and
both go out of their way to make sure Luffy

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:41.090
can go his way.

00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:51.580
Heck, Sabo actually eats Ace's devil fruit
and uses his moves.[]

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:57.169
However if you have taken away anything form
the many analysis videos I have made about

00:07:57.169 --> 00:08:02.960
One Piece, you will know that Sabo unites
two important themes Oda uses.

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:07.560
Inherited will as well as the concept of two
sides of the same coin, where most elements

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:13.550
of post-time-skip one piece are a mirrored
and inverted version of pre-time skip.

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:18.110
It's no coincidence then that Sabo appears
in Dressrosa, the arc that reflects Alabasta

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:28.199
in the first half of the grand line, where
Ace made his first appearance.

00:08:28.199 --> 00:08:32.200
Both arcs serve as setup for Luffy's relationship
with his older brothers.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:39.060
That way, Oda could set up Ace's capture at
Maarineford, and whatever happened to Sabo

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:40.060
at the reverie,

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:41.510
I'll get into that in a moment.

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:46.910
But to me, saying that these two characters
are the same is just not true.

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:50.440
Both have their distinct personalities and
differences.

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:55.460
And even strength-wise, Sabo seems a lot more
capable than ace.

00:08:55.460 --> 00:09:00.660
He wields the Mera mera no mi easily right
after eating it, is able to face off with

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:07.510
an admiral and in this scene right here, I'm
pretty sure he uses Ryouu to split the platform.[]

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:18.430
A real beast.

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:21.150
Both have their distinct emotional baggage.

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:26.710
While Ace feels unwanted and hated by the
world, Sabo blames himself for not being there

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:30.940
for Ace and Luffy when they needed him the
most.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:38.780
[sabo crushes marines mask]In his fight against
the marines he seems to go a little bit Psycho

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:44.360
for a while, until you realize that he is
just very emotional and trying to protect

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:46.750
Luffy, no matter what.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:52.410
That or he is justvery ecstatic about having
subscribed to this channel for more one piece

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:54.680
content every single week.

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:58.931
Interestingly enough, Sabo becomes a little
bit more like Ace when eating the Mera Mega

00:09:58.931 --> 00:10:02.620
no mi, even sharing the same lines as Ace.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:09.330
[sabo saying goodbye and zoro remembering
ace].

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:14.940
This could simply be a representation of Sabo
inheriting Ace's will to watch over Luffy.

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:19.340
But as I speculate in my video on Devil Fruits
here, it might very well be that devil fruits

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:24.040
themselves store a bit of their previous owners
personality in them.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:30.750
What really stands out to me though, is the
moment Luffy realizes Sabo is alive and all

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:39.390
Sabo tries to do is lessen Luffy's own burden
for not having saved Ace.

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:48.100
[] He actually thanks Luffy for being alive
like 3 or four times, making sure that Luffy

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:51.830
doesn't have any more survivors guilt about
Marine Ford.

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:57.250
And speaking of Marine Ford, there is one
really interesting detail, thatI think you

00:10:57.250 --> 00:10:58.260
will like.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:01.790
You know that Akainu's real name is actually
Sakazuki.

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:07.330
But what you might not know is, that Sakazuki
has an actual meaning in Japanese.

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:12.490
The reason his true name is so jarring is
that "Sakazuki" is the Japanese word for a

00:11:12.490 --> 00:11:18.390
pact of brotherhood over sake cups, which
is EXACTLY what Ace, Sabo, and Monkey D. Luffy

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:27.940
did to signify their brotherly bond.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:28.940
[]

00:11:28.940 --> 00:11:30.910
Why would Oda choose that name?

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:34.840
Well when you think about it for a second,
it really fits.

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:41.530
While Akainu DOES kill ace and take one sake
cup brother away from Luffy, Ace's death cures

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:47.120
Sabo's Amnesia, giving the other sake cup
brother back to him and passes his will on

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:48.120
to Sabo.

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:53.410
Sabo even states that he felt Ace's spirit
lift the fog in his mind as a way of guaranteeing

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:57.850
that Luffy always had at least one brother
looking out for him.

00:11:57.850 --> 00:12:03.820
And it might foreshadow Akainu being involved
with Sabo at some point in the story as well.

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:09.890
So, up until this point, I believe that Sabo
has already contributed a lot to Luffy and

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:11.520
to the story overall.

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:16.500
But I personally think that the most important
part of his arc is yet to come.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:31.850
And that brings us into the realm of speculation
about what happened at Marijoe to Sabo.

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:35.450
[] One possibility is of course that Sabo
has been killed.

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:40.440
That would fit in with a theory I made about
Coby inheriting the Mera Mera no mi, but even

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:44.950
if Sabo were to die, it surely wouldn't be
off-screen.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:50.810
Another, much more likely possibility, is
that Sabo has been captured and is about to

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:52.400
be executed.

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:58.690
While this would be a little bit too similar
to Ace's fate, it WOULD give Luffy the chance

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:03.550
to actually save a brother from the government
this time, which I don't hate.

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:09.380
However I personally think that Oda is trying
to trick us into believing one or the other.

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:14.820
My personal favorite idea, is that the Government
has taken out the king of alabasta, Cobra

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:18.070
and also tried to get rid of Vivi in the process.

00:13:18.070 --> 00:13:23.620
This is supported by Imu picking her image
during the reverie.

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:31.580
I think it would be quite likely that sabo
would have gone out of his way, just as he

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:35.190
saved Rebecca on Dressrosa and running away
with her.

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:40.190
As a result, the government could have blamed
Cobra's death on Sabo, but would still want

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:46.870
to keep the news from spreading that a revolutionary
was able to infiltrate and escape Marijo without

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:51.930
being caught.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:56.980
Remember this scene?

00:13:56.980 --> 00:14:07.030
[] Sabo has a vivre card of Luffy and Vivi
is bound to return to the crew.

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:12.090
So if both of them escaped together from Marijoe
and Sabo can sense Luffy's vivre card burning

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:16.360
up during his fight with on Wano, it would
make sense for the pair to make their way

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:21.280
towards the straw hats, maybe bringing the
rest of the revolutionary army along to battle

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:23.860
the marines coming to Wano as well.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:28.300
Sabo reuniting with Luffy would have an additional
meaning as well.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:31.350
Remember how all his attacks are dragon based?

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:35.880
Well, Sabo is literally the right hand of
Dragon himself.

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:40.530
And we know that Luffy has no relationship
with his father at all.

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:45.580
However, Sabo was raised by dragon instead
and he grew up with Luffy.

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:50.150
So who better to bring these two together
than Luffy's older brother.

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:55.341
And one other thing I would really love to
see, is Sabo and Luffy visiting Ace's grave

00:14:55.341 --> 00:14:57.770
together at the end of the story.

00:14:57.770 --> 00:15:03.210
Or, if Luffy doesn't make it, Sabo visiting
both of their graves next to each other.

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:08.480
I don't know why, but I just thinking about
that scene at the end of one piece, already

00:15:08.480 --> 00:15:10.270
puts tears in my eyes.

00:15:10.270 --> 00:15:14.340
If you don't want to cry now, and rather learn
why devil fruits may have a will of their

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:19.740
own and why Sabo might have inherited Ace's
will by eating his devil fruit, just click

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:21.310
right on my face.

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:25.750
I swear my eyes are just sweating.

